2. Individual plan: free personal, noncommercial use

An individual natural person may download, install, run, copy and modify
Diffrook without paying a license fee solely for that person's private,
personal, noncommercial activities. Each Individual installation is limited
to one registered user account and three saved automations. Disabled
automations also count toward the limit. Multiple accounts, shared accounts
and splitting an organizational deployment into personal installations do not
qualify as Individual use.

The Individual plan has no license fee for permitted use, with no expiry or
trial period. SSO is not included for new Individual identities. The person
provides their own server and AI provider or local model. Infrastructure and
AI charges are separate from the free software license.

The Individual plan does not permit use for a company, organization or team,
or use in employment, freelance work, consulting, client work or other
professional or commercial activities, even when only one person uses
Diffrook or no fee is charged for a particular task. Those uses require a
Business license, except for the limited free beta authorization below. The
user's own hosting, infrastructure and AI-provider costs remain the user's
responsibility.

3. Business plan: paid self-hosted use

Companies, organizations, teams and individuals performing professional or
commercial work must obtain a separate paid Business license from the
licensors before operating Diffrook for those purposes, except where the free beta authorization below applies. A Business
license authorizes self-hosted use only within the customer, installation,
user, automation and term limits specified in the
applicable written commercial agreement. Fees, duration, renewal, support and
any service commitments are determined by that agreement; no particular price,
perpetual entitlement, support level or unlimited allowance is promised here.

The paid self-hosted subscription plans are:
- Freelancer: one registered user and ten saved automations, for individual
  professional use, with local sign-in and without SSO.
- Teams: purchased registered users, from one to ten, and twenty saved
  automations per purchased user, pooled across the installation, including
  SSO and use within the licensed organization.
- Enterprise: purchased registered users, with a minimum of ten, and twenty
  saved automations per purchased user, pooled across the installation,
  including SSO. Additional packs of ten automations may be arranged.

Paid subscriptions renew monthly or annually and include software updates
during their term. Published prices and annual discounts are described in
docs/licensing.md and the embedded plan catalog. Payment and renewal must be
arranged with the licensors; a license request is not payment or activation.
Customers provide their own hosting and AI. Self-hosted subscriptions do not
charge by execution. No support response time or availability SLA is included
unless explicitly agreed in writing. Previously issued Business license files
remain recognized under their original terms and technical allowances.

A signed license file activates the purchased installation's technical
entitlements. Possessing source code, setting an environment variable,
altering the database or disabling a technical check does not grant a Business
license. Technical limits do not replace the restrictions in these terms or
the applicable commercial agreement. Specific terms in a signed commercial
agreement prevail over conflicting terms in this license for that customer.

On expiry or removal of a Business license, its additional technical creation
allowances cease. Stored data is not automatically deleted. Continued access
for reading, editing, deleting or exporting existing data does not extend a
customer's contractual entitlement to operate Diffrook for business use.
Previously provisioned SSO identities may retain verified sign-in access for
data recovery; this does not include provisioning new SSO identities or extend
a subscription's contractual term.

3a. Limited free self-hosted beta authorization

Official Diffrook beta builds designated for this offer allow Individual,
Freelancer and Teams to be used without paying a license fee during the beta
program. Individual remains limited to personal, noncommercial use with one
user and three saved automations. Freelancer permits professional and commercial
self-hosted use by one user with ten saved automations and without SSO. Teams
permits self-hosted use within one organization by up to ten registered users
with two hundred saved automations and OIDC SSO. Disabled automations count.

Enterprise, extra automation packs and Cloud Hosting are excluded. The offer
requires no payment card, signed paid license or recurring subscription, and
creates no automatic charge. Customers provide and pay for their own server
and AI. The restrictions on hosting for third parties, redistribution,
modifications, warranties and other terms of this license continue to apply.

This authorization applies only to designated official beta builds and ends
with the beta program when the first official stable release is published. It
does not grant a perpetual Freelancer or Teams license, access to stable
releases for professional use, Enterprise rights or any service commitment.
Official stable releases require a separately purchased signed license for
Freelancer, Teams or Enterprise. Individual remains free forever for permitted
personal, noncommercial use. Upgrading does not create a subscription or charge
without a separate purchase. Existing customer agreements remain effective.

4. Hosted subscriptions and third-party hosting

The licensors may offer a separately paid subscription in which they host and
operate Diffrook for the customer. A hosted subscription is distinct
from a self-hosted Business license. Availability, features, infrastructure,
usage limits, pricing, billing, data handling, support and termination are
subject to a separate hosted-service agreement. This license does not promise
that a hosted service is currently available or included in a self-hosted fee.

Cloud Hosting is currently marked "Coming soon". Its displayed plans, AI token
rates and execution allowances describe the intended offering and do not
provide an available service or purchase entitlement. All planned hosted plans
are paid monthly or annually. Customers may supply their own AI credentials
or, once offered, pay monthly for managed AI consumption. Subscription discounts
do not discount managed AI consumption. Hosted data isolation, backups, usage
controls and billing require the hosted service to be launched separately.

Operating, reselling or offering Diffrook as a hosted or managed service for
third parties requires separate written authorization from the licensors.
Neither the Individual plan nor a standard self-hosted Business license grants
that right. The licensors' own authorized hosted offerings are permitted.

